cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "nir-eye-cam"
abstract: >-
  Small near-infrared cameras for mouse pupil and eye imaging. Firmware for a
  Himax HM01B0 camera on an RP2040 board and for an ST VD55G1 global-shutter
  sensor on an ESP32-P4, both streaming 8-bit frames over USB, and a Python
  recorder that puts several free-running cameras on one timeline by
  timestamping a shared sync line.
authors:
  - given-names: "Stefan N."
    family-names: "Oline"
    affiliation: "Princeton University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7094-3800"
version: "0.1.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/olinesn/nir-eye-cam"
# The project's license is not an SPDX identifier, which CFF's `license`
# field requires, so it is linked instead.
license-url: "https://github.com/olinesn/nir-eye-cam/blob/main/LICENSE"
keywords:
  - near-infrared imaging
  - pupillometry
  - eye tracking
  - mouse
  - camera firmware
  - RP2040
  - ESP32-P4
  - multi-camera synchronization
